<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{.language}}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{.title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{.description}}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{.url}}">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{.url}}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{.title}}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{.description}}">
<meta property="og:image" content="{{.socialImage.src}}">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{.socialImage.alt}}">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="preload" href="assets/fonts/tektur-var.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="assets/fonts/martian-mono-var.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#04070b">
<script>document.documentElement.classList.add("js")</script>
{{style "assets/styles/main.css"}}
</head>
<body>
<header class="top">
  <a class="brand" href="{{.url}}">GhostPaw</a>
  <nav aria-label="Site">
    <a href="#libraries">Libraries</a>
    <a href="#fit">How they fit</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.githubOrg}}">GitHub</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.npmOrg}}">npm</a>
  </nav>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Your agent keeps its state in markdown files.</h1>
      <p class="lede"><code>MEMORY.md</code>, <code>TODO.md</code>, <code>USER.md</code>, <code>SOUL.md</code>. They grow every session, nobody prunes them, and one wrong line steers every run after it.</p>
      <p>GhostPaw is seven small Node.js libraries, one for each of those files and for the skills, inbox and chats around them. Each keeps its part of the state as SQLite records inside your agent's own process, so you can read, correct and delete what the agent knows while it runs without you.</p>
      <div class="install">
        <label for="hero-cmd">Start with memory</label>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="hero-cmd" readonly value="npm install @ghostpaw/codex" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="hero-cmd">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <p class="actions"><a class="button" href="#libraries">See all seven</a> <a href="#fit">How they fit together</a></p>
      <p class="terms">Free, MIT licence, Node.js 24 or newer. All seven have zero runtime dependencies. No account and no service to run.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-art frame">
      <div class="scope"><picture><source media="(min-width: 52rem)" srcset="assets/images/hero-720.webp" width="720" height="540"><img src="assets/images/hero-480.webp" width="480" height="360" alt="A wolf head in profile drawn in thin cyan light lines, dissolving into violet sparks on black." fetchpriority="high"></picture><span class="scan" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <p class="readout" aria-label="Zero runtime dependencies in all seven packages"><span class="big">0</span><span>runtime dependencies</span><small>in all seven packages</small></p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="libraries" class="libs" aria-labelledby="libs-title">
    <h2 id="libs-title">One library for each file your agent keeps</h2>
    <p class="intro">Each row names the file it takes over, what it gives an agent that runs with nobody watching, and the one command that installs it.</p>
    <ol class="lib-rows">
      {{range .data.packages}}<li class="lib-row" id="lib-{{.name}}">
        <p class="lib-file"><span>Replaces</span> <code>{{.file}}</code></p>
        <div class="lib-main">
          <h3><a href="{{index $.urls .page}}">{{.name}}</a> <span class="ver">{{.version}}</span></h3>
          <p class="lib-role">{{.role}}</p>
          <p class="lib-gives">{{.gives}}</p>
          <p class="lib-holds">One record holds:</p>
          <ul class="lib-fields">{{range .fields}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul>
        </div>
        <div class="lib-act">
          <div class="cmd"><input id="cmd-{{.key}}" readonly value="npm install {{.pkg}}" aria-label="Install command for {{.name}}" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="cmd-{{.key}}">Copy</button></div>
          <p class="links"><a class="more" href="{{index $.urls .page}}">The {{.name}} page</a><a href="{{index $.urls .docs}}">{{.docsLabel}}</a><a href="{{index $.urls .gh}}">{{.name}} on GitHub</a></p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {{end}}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="fit" class="fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <h2 id="fit-title">How they fit together</h2>
    <p class="intro">The packages never import each other. Your agent's code carries data from one to the next, and each keeps its own records, in its own tables.</p>
    <p class="intro">Here is one afternoon of an agent that runs a small renewal desk on its own.</p>
    <div class="fit-grid">
    <ol class="run">
      {{range .data.run}}<li class="run-step"><p class="run-lib"><code>{{.lib}}</code></p><p class="run-what">{{.what}}</p></li>
      {{end}}
    </ol>
    <figure class="tracks">
      <figcaption>What the afternoon left on disk</figcaption>
      <p class="tracks-root"><code>~/.ghostpaw/</code></p>
      <ul>{{range .data.run}}<li><code>{{.file}}</code><span>{{.lands}}</span></li>{{end}}</ul>
    </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="note">An illustration of one way to wire them, not a recorded run. Each library's own page replays a real run against its current release.</p>
    <h3 class="shape-title">What all seven share</h3>
    <dl class="shape">
      <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Node.js 24 or newer and its built-in <code>node:sqlite</code>. Zero runtime dependencies, MIT licence.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Ways in</dt><dd>A library import, an MCP server started with <code>npx -y @ghostpaw/&lt;name&gt; mcp</code>, a <code>ghostpaw-&lt;name&gt;</code> command line tool and an Agent Skill.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Where state lives</dt><dd>A SQLite file you can open. The MCP servers default to <code>~/.ghostpaw/&lt;name&gt;.db</code>; grimoire also keeps its SKILL.md files in a git folder.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Taking one</dt><dd>Install one package and ignore the rest. None of them needs another to work.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="worry" aria-labelledby="worry-title">
    <h2 id="worry-title">If an agent working alone worries you</h2>
    <div class="worry-grid">
    <div class="worry-lead"><p>Plenty of developers switch agent memory off, because unread memories pile up and old lines win arguments, and an agent that also sends mail, posts in groups and rewrites its own instructions while you sleep is a bigger worry than one that only remembers.</p>
    <p>Here is what each package does about it.</p></div>
    <ul>
      <li>Every record is a row in a SQLite file your own process opens. You can read and delete it with <code>sqlite3</code>.</li>
      <li>codex flags a belief nobody confirms for 90 days as stale, and recall calls no model.</li>
      <li>questlog's <code>run_quest</code> tool refuses to start a quest whose prerequisites are unmet, unless the call passes <code>force</code>.</li>
      <li>email keeps reading and sending in separate tools. Leave <code>mail_compose</code> out and the agent cannot send.</li>
      <li>telegram's send and moderation tools return plans until you switch execution on.</li>
      <li>souls and grimoire keep every change to identity and skills as history you can roll back.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="all" aria-labelledby="all-title">
    <div class="all-head">
    <h2 id="all-title">All seven, side by side</h2>
    <img class="trail" src="assets/images/art-640.webp" width="640" height="360" alt="Four paw prints in light walking up and to the right, the oldest fading violet, the newest bright cyan." loading="lazy">
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption>The seven GhostPaw packages and what we measured</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Takes over</th><th scope="col">Version</th><th scope="col">Runtime deps</th><th scope="col">Tests</th><th scope="col">gzip</th><th scope="col">Import</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {{range .data.packages}}<tr><th scope="row"><a href="{{index $.urls .page}}"><code>{{.pkg}}</code></a></th><td data-label="Takes over"><code>{{.file}}</code></td><td data-label="Version">{{.version}}</td><td data-label="Runtime deps">{{.deps}}</td><td data-label="Tests">{{.tests}}</td><td data-label="gzip">{{.gzip}}</td><td data-label="Import">{{.importMs}}</td></tr>{{end}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">{{.data.measured}}</p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="foot">
  <nav class="foot-libs" aria-label="GhostPaw libraries">{{range .data.packages}}<a href="{{index $.urls .page}}">{{.name}}</a>{{end}}</nav>
  <p>GhostPaw is maintained in the open under the MIT licence. Every number on this page comes from the repositories and npm.</p>
  <p class="foot-links">
    <a href="{{.urls.githubOrg}}">GhostPawJS on GitHub</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.npmOrg}}">@ghostpaw on npm</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.impressum}}">Impressum</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.privacy}}">Datenschutz</a>
  </p>
</footer>
{{script "assets/scripts/main.js"}}
</body>
</html>
